      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "Some pilots, at the critical moment, switch off their targeting computer and go with their gut. Yours now tells the time — so maybe leave it on.\n\nA wireframe tunnel. Red range lines closing in. A crosshair that locks on and holds. Stay On Target turns your Apple Watch into a 1970s vector targeting display, with the time underneath in a big angular red readout. It is, technically, a clock.\n\nSpin the crown and the radio crackles — short pilot callouts, recorded for this app.\n\nTap the date and your week scrolls away into the distance as a text crawl: today, tomorrow, and every day after that with something on it. Drag it with a finger or spin the crown to move through at your own pace. Nothing booked? It says so, and it sounds pleased for you.\n\nWHAT IT DOES\n\n- Always-on display: the clock keeps time while the animation rests\n- Amber or phosphor green — tap to switch cockpits\n- Radio callouts on the crown, silenced with one tap when you're in a meeting and your wrist starts talking\n- Mission Briefing: your week's appointments as a receding crawl — drag or spin to scrub through it\n- Rings, steps, resting heart rate and last night's sleep, read straight off the watch\n- 12 or 24 hour, whichever way you were trained\n- Runs entirely on the watch. No phone app, no account, no setup\n- Collects nothing. We genuinely have no idea who you are\n\nTip: Settings → General → Return to Clock → 1 hour. Now it stays up like a real watch face every time you raise your wrist.\n\nDon't get cocky.\n\nhttps://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/",
